### LAB 4.

### 1. GET All items (gets CSRF token)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Accept: application/json

> {%
  client.global.set("xsrf", response.headers.valueOf("X-XSRF-TOKEN"));
  client.test("1. Show all", () => client.assert(response.status === 200));
%}


### 2. POST create one
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items
Authorization: Basic admin admin
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Book", "description": "CSRF test" }

> {%
  client.global.set("id", response.body.id);
  client.test("2. Create one", () => client.assert(response.status === 201));
%}


### 3. GET read one
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Accept: application/json

> {% client.test("3. Read one", () => client.assert(response.status === 200)); %}


### 4. PUT update one
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic admin admin
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Book v2", "description": "Updated" }

> {% client.test("4. Update one", () => client.assert(response.status === 200)); %}


### 5. DELETE delete one
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic admin admin
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}

> {% client.test("5. Delete one", () => client.assert(response.status === 204)); %}
